// PLAYTEST: is a Bastion's buff worth a round of not attacking?
//
// One of five files — `player-class-striker`, `-bastion`, `-medic`,
// `-saboteur`, `-leech` — identical in every field but `character`. See
// `player-class-striker.ron` for the shared argument: why the pack is this
// pack, why the pool is unspent, and why **the headless bin reports the same
// numbers for all five** (it plays All-Attack and invokes nothing, so it is
// the floor rather than the measurement).
//
//     FERAL_DEV_ARENA=1 cargo run  ->  [R] Arena  ->  [L] player-class-bastion
//
// The floor, 2026-09-01, 20 reps, seeds 1-20: 60% won, mean 18.6 rounds,
// 26% player Integrity left, 1.15 companions down. Compare deltas within one
// build only.
//
// A buff is the hardest of the five to feel, and this is the file that
// should say so if it is true. Hyperthread Single grants +6 Attack for four
// rounds at 1.3, so it pays back only in a fight with rounds left to spend
// it over — which is why this pack runs long. A 19-round fight is close to
// the best case a buff will ever get.
//
// What to watch:
//   - The break-even. Four rounds of +6 Attack against one round of not
//     attacking: does the fight visibly shorten, or is it inside the noise
//     of the damage band?
//   - Whom you put it on. It is single-target, so a Bastion is choosing
//     between themselves and a companion every time — is that a decision or
//     an obvious answer?
//   - Bastion damps Damage at 0.8, and this kit has no damage routine to
//     damp, so the trade is invisible here by construction. That is the
//     finding if the class reads as a free bonus.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 5, zone: 1),
    character: (
        class: Some(Bastion),
        stats: (0, 0, 0, 0),
        routine: Some("hyperthread"),
    ),
    party: [
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
    ],
    reps: 1,
    seed: 2,
)
